# A name bound to what the language's own code computes of names, with no call, stands for those names (#328), and
# the body's own code reads those names where it reads the name, never where it binds it (#343): `named` binds the gap
# between the level and the module's quiet level (`first.db - QUIET.db`) and the list of both (`[first, QUIET]`) to names
# before it hands each to a step, and `written` writes each where its step is handed it. An operator is no occurrence and
# a name adds no arrow, so the two routes are one plan: each step takes the level and the quiet level, which alone comes
# from beyond, and the route's own arrow reads neither where the body binds a name to them.

route signal.named
step named/_draw
step named/_show

line entry > named call
line Level·first > named value
line Level·first > named/_draw value                 # `_draw(gap)`, `gap = first.db - QUIET.db`
line Level·QUIET > named/_draw value                 # the module's quiet level, from beyond
line Level·first > named/_show value                 # `_show(both)`, `both = [first, QUIET]`
line Level·QUIET > named/_show value
line named/_draw > Screen own
line named/_show > Screen own

home Level·first named
home Level·QUIET named

side entry left
side Screen right

route signal.written
step written/_draw
step written/_show

line entry > written call
line Level·first > written value
line Level·first > written/_draw value               # `_draw(first.db - QUIET.db)`
line Level·QUIET > written/_draw value
line Level·first > written/_show value               # `_show([first, QUIET])`
line Level·QUIET > written/_show value
line written/_draw > Screen own
line written/_show > Screen own

home Level·first written
home Level·QUIET written

side entry left
side Screen right
